.title  The ground becomes a surface: the painter, the first crash, and a word that overflows
.what   Every square of the lattice is filled now, painted far to near so each one covers what was behind it - the painter's algorithm, which is lesson 15's table read backwards. The skyline array and five line routines are gone. A filled hillside ends the flight. Twice the view distance overflowed a 16-bit word when the square block turned 45 degrees, so the view became a circle. Then three speed-ups, each measured: 19 to 27 frames, and one of them bought almost nothing
.tier   LESSON
.main   FILL.ASM
.build  FASM FILL.ASM FILL.COM
.run    FILL.COM
.uses   IMUL IDIV SAR SHR AND OR TEST LODSB STOSW MOVSW REP NOP CMP JGE JAE IN OUT CLI STI IRET
